<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Kemin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Kemin was a Chinese banker and former finance minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-government">Beiyang government</a> who collaborated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> after its invasion of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. In December 1937 he became head of the Provisional Government of the Republic of China in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, which in 1940 was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a>'s Reorganized National Government. Arrested as a traitor after the war, he died in prison in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wang-kemin.jpg" alt="Wang Kemin" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown; scanned by 天竺鼠 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wang_Kemin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
